   </property>
   <property name="toolTip">
    <string>&lt;html&gt;&lt;head/&gt;&lt;body&gt;&lt;p&gt;DEFAULT - CV1 = GATE, CV2 = PITCH. If multiple notes are assigned to a 12 Step Key, only the first note (the one in the top of the editor) controls CV. Any USB MIDI note on/off messages sent to the 12 Step will also control gate/pitch. For all other CV settings described below, USB MIDI Note on/off messages are ignored.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;GATE - the CV is set to 5V when a key is pressed, and 0V when the key is released.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;PITCH - the CV is set to a (1V/Oct) voltage that matches the most recent key that was pressed.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;PRESSURE - the CV is set to 0-5V corresponding to the current PRESSURE of the active key &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;TILT - the CV is set to 0-5V corresponding to the current TILT of the active key &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;PEDAL - the CV is set to 0-5V, controlled by the expression pedal input &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;USB CH15 or USB CH16 - the CV is only controlled by USB MIDI messages, either Pitch Bend (14bit scaled to 12bit 0-5V) or Control Changes (7bit scaled to 12bit 0-5V) &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Note - CV features are only available on 12 Step2, and are disabled if legacy hardware is connected.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;</string>
   </property>
   <property name="styleSheet">
